        "orario": "17:30",
        "timestamp": 1776439808,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Macron urges permanent reopening of Hormuz Strait France Issued on: 17/04/2026 - 17:30 Modified: 17/04/2026 - 17:30 French President Emmanuel Macron and British Prime Minister Keir Starmer on Friday hosted a video conference with their European allies to discuss the possible deployment of a multinational force to the Strait of Hormuz once the war in Iran is over. Macron welcomed Iran's announcement that the waterway would be reopened to commercial shipping for the rest of the ceasefire, but called for the strait's \"unconditional\" reopening. Starmer, Macron push forward efforts to reopen Strait of Hormuz 17/04/2026 France Britain, France chair meeting on Hormuz 17/04/2026 France Strait of Hormuz: Macron, Starmer meet at Elysée Palace 17/04/2026 France Europe leads postwar security talks 17/04/2026 Europe France, UK host talks on securing Hormuz 17/04/2026 France French billionaire Bolloré sparks turmoil at Grasset as 115 authors leave publishing house 16/04/2026 France Debate on French bill outlawing ‘new forms of anti-Semitism' pushed back 16/04/2026 France Antisemitism and apology for terrorism 'already illegal in France': Is Yadan Law 'really necessary?' 16/04/2026 France French MPs introduce bill to remove statute of limitations for crimes against children 15/04/2026 France"
